Databinding
---------------------
Data-binding means  it is a process of access the data from
data source(variables,arrays,objects,api,databases) render on the ui.
In javascript you want implement the data databinding you have to use
lot of dom methods and dom properties.

But in react data binding is managed by only binding expression that is
"{}"

In react data-binding is divided into two types

1.one-way binding
2.two-way binding

one-way binding:
----------------
one-way binding means access the data from data soucre render on the ui.
----------------
one-way binding means access the data from data soucre render on the ui.
but by default react support one way binding.

two-way binding:
----------------
two-way binding means access the data from data soucre render on the ui.
it identify the changes on the ui updated to data source.


Javascript
----------
let message="Good morning";

<p id="p1"></p>
document.getElementById("p1").innerText=message;

React
----------
<h1>{message}</h1>
<p>{message}</p>

 useState Hook(FAQ)
----------------------
The useState() hook is one of the most important hooks in React. It is used to create and manage state (data) inside functional components.

useState() is a React Hook that allows us to store data in a functional component and update that data whenever required.

const [state, setState] = useState(initialValue);

state=>variable
setState=>method for update the state data
useState()=> function for store the data


List Rendering in React:
---------------------------------

"Accessing the elements of a JavaScript array and displaying them in an ordered or structured format on the UI is called List Rendering in React."

In React List Rendering, each repeated item should be identified by a unique key prop.
"React uses the unique key prop to identify individual elements in a list and efficiently update the UI when elements are added, modified, or deleted."